WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.166
Two documented incidents
show why the whole-agency

2
00:00:03.166 --> 00:00:06.500
view is a security property,
not a reporting preference.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.558
In May and June 2023, an actor
used a Microsoft consumer

4
00:00:10.558 --> 00:00:14.887
signing key to forge tokens
and read Exchange Online mail.

5
00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:20.119
The Cyber Safety Review Board counted
22 enterprise organizations and 503

6
00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:25.600
related personal accounts, with access to
some mailboxes for at least six weeks.

7
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.825
The tokens were valid to every
system that checked them.

8
00:00:28.825 --> 00:00:31.848
What caught the intrusion
was a custom alert one

9
00:00:31.848 --> 00:00:35.400
federal department had built
on mailbox logs it paid for.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.462
The second sits beneath the guest.

11
00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:43.949
ESXiArgs compromised more than
3,800 ESXi servers in February 2023.

12
00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:49.522
In 2024, CVE-2024-37085 gave
full hypervisor control to

13
00:00:49.522 --> 00:00:55.837
members of a directory group
named ESX Admins, matched by name.

14
00:00:55.837 --> 00:00:58.399
Even one vendor's two tools don't add up.

15
00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:02.533
ScubaGear is CISA's, the Zero
Trust Assessment is Microsoft's,

16
00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:05.450
and neither sees past
Microsoft's platform.

17
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.162
Tools are evidence inputs.

18
00:01:07.162 --> 00:01:09.380
The agency owns the verdict.
